flowchart TB
  accTitle: Filtering and failure behaviour
  accDescr: SMTP mail and new collector imports are checked for malware. Clean mail is scored with conventional rules and an AI signal. Scores of five or more go to Junk. If AI is unavailable, SMTP uses conventional filtering and collectors defer and retry. Malware and scanner failures do not bypass protection.
  Source["SMTP mail or new collector import"] --> AV{"ClamAV"}
  AV -->|Malware| Block["Block delivery"]:::warning
  AV -->|Scanner unavailable| Retry["Defer and retry"]:::warning
  AV -->|Clean| Rules["Conventional spam signals"]
  Rules --> AI["Bounded AI classification<br/>2 workers + short queue"]:::core
  AI -->|Verdict| Score{"Combined score ≥ 5?"}
  AI -. Unavailable: SMTP .-> Fallback["Conventional score only"] --> Score
  AI -. Unavailable: collector .-> Retry
  Score -->|Yes| Junk["Junk"]:::warning
  Score -->|No| Inbox["Inbox"]:::good

  classDef core fill:#d92650,color:#ffffff,stroke:#b91c45,stroke-width:2px
  classDef store fill:#eff6ff,color:#1e3a5f,stroke:#93b4d5
  classDef good fill:#ecfdf5,color:#14532d,stroke:#86b99e
  classDef warning fill:#fff1f2,color:#9f1239,stroke:#e8a3b4
